"answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative led by Marcus Cole, with a kickoff scheduled for July 15th, 2023. The project has progressed through several phases, including design and development (led by Omar Jensen), and recently completed its testing phase ahead of schedule, achieving a major milestone with a successfully tested secure file sharing prototype. To support this growth, five new team members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture are joining, with an onboarding session set for September 10th. The next phase involves user interface enhancements starting in October, followed by a celebration of the testing milestone on October 10th. Stakeholder feedback on the prototype is being sought by the end of November. Looking ahead, security protocols will be updated in January to include multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest. Additionally, the compliance plan budget has been increased to $55,000, and the team is exploring a potential partnership with TechInnovate for AI technology integration."
